# Byte-exact attachments, on every platform.
#
# The pipeline reads the organisers' documents as bytes, and a PDF's xref
# table is a table of byte offsets. A PDF-1.3 file from their generator can
# contain no NUL byte at all, so git's text heuristic calls it text, and a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true then rewrites every LF to CRLF:
# `startxref` points 74 bytes short, pdfplumber reports "Unexpected EOF", and
# email_499_BL.pdf -- a real planted defect on gross_weight_kg -- was read as
# an unreadable attachment on this platform only (docs/STATUS.md 2026-09-24,
# the 45/21 vs 46/20 discrepancy). Thirty-four committed PDFs were exposed to
# that conversion; one broke. Declaring every binary format here means no
# checkout, on any OS, can alter a byte of what the readers are measured on.
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.pptx  binary
